WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:01.410
- Hello, everyone.

00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:02.510
Welcome to another coffee break

00:00:02.510 --> 00:00:04.550
here on my channel, Firm Learning.

00:00:04.550 --> 00:00:07.520
Today, I wanna talk about the
terrible events in Ukraine,

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:09.820
and how this affects consulting firms,

00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:11.967
and especially the Russian business

00:00:11.967 --> 00:00:14.330
of the consulting firms around the world.

00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:15.920
After Russia invading Ukraine,

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:17.917
you see many organizations
around the world

00:00:17.917 --> 00:00:20.940
who speak up and take
actions by, for instance,

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:22.469
stopping business in Russia.

00:00:22.469 --> 00:00:24.940
Does this the case for the
consulting firms as well?

00:00:24.940 --> 00:00:27.900
And what are maybe differences
among the different firms

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:30.270
in how they react to the Russian business?

00:00:30.270 --> 00:00:32.640
And of course, what does this imply

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:35.770
for the employees working in
these Russian organizations?

00:00:35.770 --> 00:00:38.480
So this is what I wanna talk
about today in this video.

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:41.320
I will donate all the YouTube ad revenue

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:44.513
that I receive from
this video to the UNHCR,

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:47.550
which is the UN agency mandated

00:00:47.550 --> 00:00:50.020
to aid and protect
refugees around the world.

00:00:50.020 --> 00:00:52.320
They're currently also active in Ukraine.

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:53.460
So if you watch the video,

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:54.900
it will directly contribute to that

00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:57.340
if you watch the ads and
watch until the very end.

00:00:57.340 --> 00:00:59.400
Thank you very much for
your support on this.

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:01.060
So in order to put together this video,

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:03.890
I did some desk research,
read lots of press statements,

00:01:03.890 --> 00:01:05.380
also statements on LinkedIn

00:01:05.380 --> 00:01:06.357
that many consulting firms

00:01:06.357 --> 00:01:08.830
and the leaders of these firms published.

00:01:08.830 --> 00:01:11.430
And I reached out to you on Instagram,

00:01:11.430 --> 00:01:13.770
asking for your firsthand impressions,

00:01:13.770 --> 00:01:15.480
firsthand insider knowledge,

00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:17.980
on what is going on in
all these consulting firms

00:01:17.980 --> 00:01:20.940
and what they're doing with
their Russian organizations.

00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:23.903
So thanks so much for all the
messages that I did receive.

00:01:23.903 --> 00:01:25.190
I do wanna say, as a disclaimer,

00:01:25.190 --> 00:01:27.440
that first, the situation
is dynamically evolving.

00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:29.440
So potentially the information
I'm sharing right now

00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:30.360
is not accurate anymore

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:32.060
in a couple of days or a couple of weeks.

00:01:32.060 --> 00:01:33.730
And second, because
lots of the information

00:01:33.730 --> 00:01:36.700
I'm sharing in this video is
from you, from the community,

00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:38.590
I have no direct way of verifying it.

00:01:38.590 --> 00:01:40.560
Though if any of you proves me wrong,

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:44.000
that anything I say as
of today is not accurate

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:46.060
I will include a pinned post

00:01:46.060 --> 00:01:49.070
in the comment section
with any clarifications

00:01:49.070 --> 00:01:51.360
or any amendments or
corrections of what I'm saying.

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:52.250
So let's get started.

00:01:52.250 --> 00:01:53.830
And first of all, I think it's fair to say

00:01:53.830 --> 00:01:56.240
that the whole situation did leave a mark

00:01:56.240 --> 00:01:58.030
on the consulting industry.

00:01:58.030 --> 00:02:01.310
Lots of firms did take action
the moment we go firm by firm,

00:02:01.310 --> 00:02:03.990
from any of the major firms,
what exactly they did.

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:06.840
There even was a statement
from Oleksandr Kravchenko

00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:10.620
which was the managing
director of McKinsey in Ukraine

00:02:10.620 --> 00:02:12.650
who released a post on LinkedIn saying

00:02:12.650 --> 00:02:16.610
that the Russian actions
were a military crime.

00:02:16.610 --> 00:02:19.070
So from my experience such
a candid political statement

00:02:19.070 --> 00:02:22.200
is rather rare from leadership
of any big consulting firm.

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:24.130
As far as I know that
person who has uttered that

00:02:24.130 --> 00:02:25.240
as a private person,

00:02:25.240 --> 00:02:28.100
not necessarily as an official
spokesperson for the firm.

00:02:28.100 --> 00:02:30.020
But still this reaction is remarkable,

00:02:30.020 --> 00:02:31.980
and surely nothing like everyday business

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:33.020
what's going on right now.

00:02:33.020 --> 00:02:34.560
But let's look into individual firms,

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:37.930
and let's start with the MBB
strategy consulting firms.

00:02:37.930 --> 00:02:39.900
So McKinsey, BCG, and Bain.

00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:41.540
Shortly after the news of the invasion,

00:02:41.540 --> 00:02:43.280
McKinsey released a statement saying

00:02:43.280 --> 00:02:46.330
that they will not any work
for the Russian government.

00:02:46.330 --> 00:02:47.550
And then a couple of days later

00:02:47.550 --> 00:02:50.990
they extended that to not
accepting any new work

00:02:50.990 --> 00:02:53.110
for any Russian client whatsoever.

00:02:53.110 --> 00:02:55.250
And rather similar
statements were released

00:02:55.250 --> 00:02:56.100
by the leadership

00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:58.500
of Boston Consulting Group and of Bain.

00:02:58.500 --> 00:02:59.750
But what exactly does this mean

00:02:59.750 --> 00:03:02.517
for the staff of these
organizations working in Russia?

00:03:02.517 --> 00:03:04.260
And once again, I wanna reiterate that all

00:03:04.260 --> 00:03:06.720
of this information was
collected from the community.

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:08.840
I wasn't able to verify any of it.

00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:10.720
Feel free to leave a
comment if you know more.

00:03:10.720 --> 00:03:12.480
And apparently for McKinsey, the situation

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:14.490
is that many colleagues got transferred

00:03:14.490 --> 00:03:16.320
to the Kazakhstan office.

00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:18.450
And from there, they
will conduct lion work

00:03:18.450 --> 00:03:20.630
for especially middle Eastern clients,

00:03:20.630 --> 00:03:22.830
but then also other
international projects.

00:03:22.830 --> 00:03:25.830
And I know from at least
one instance where an offer

00:03:25.830 --> 00:03:28.320
that a candidate received
during the interview process

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:30.540
was postponed by Boston Consulting Group.

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:31.430
They seemed to be in the middle

00:03:31.430 --> 00:03:35.080
of the process of relocating
consultants to other offices.

00:03:35.080 --> 00:03:36.900
So the process seemed to be more top down,

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:39.010
not necessarily only
focused on one office,

00:03:39.010 --> 00:03:39.843
but more depending

00:03:39.843 --> 00:03:42.090
on the individual situation
of the consultants.

00:03:42.090 --> 00:03:42.923
And here I've been told that,

00:03:42.923 --> 00:03:45.870
especially for some juniors
this process poses some issues.

00:03:45.870 --> 00:03:47.970
So far it does not seem to
be clear what will happen

00:03:47.970 --> 00:03:50.640
to the colleagues that will
not able to make this switch

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:52.810
to make this transition to another office.

00:03:52.810 --> 00:03:54.500
Bain seems to have transferred a good part

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:56.670
of their consultants to the Dubai office,

00:03:56.670 --> 00:03:58.240
and then helping them to get staff

00:03:58.240 --> 00:03:59.500
to international projects,

00:03:59.500 --> 00:04:01.020
also projects in the middle east.

00:04:01.020 --> 00:04:01.940
As with the other firms

00:04:01.940 --> 00:04:03.380
there seems to be an ongoing process

00:04:03.380 --> 00:04:05.724
but I have been told by
sources from all of these firms

00:04:05.724 --> 00:04:09.350
that so far there was no
layoff directly related

00:04:09.350 --> 00:04:10.840
to the situation in Ukraine.

00:04:10.840 --> 00:04:12.040
Next is Oliver Wyman.

00:04:12.040 --> 00:04:14.070
And while the Oliver
Wyman leadership stated

00:04:14.070 --> 00:04:15.260
that they don't want to conduct

00:04:15.260 --> 00:04:17.110
any more client work in Russia,

00:04:17.110 --> 00:04:19.920
there was a press release
from Marsh McLennan

00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:22.720
which is the company
that owns Oliver Wyman

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:26.040
that said, we intend to transfer ownership

00:04:26.040 --> 00:04:27.850
of our Russian businesses

00:04:27.850 --> 00:04:31.470
to local management who
will operate independently

00:04:31.470 --> 00:04:32.660
in the Russian market.

00:04:32.660 --> 00:04:34.730
So what this means is,
and I got this confirmed

00:04:34.730 --> 00:04:35.960
from some local sources,

00:04:35.960 --> 00:04:37.800
that what apparently they're trying to do

00:04:37.800 --> 00:04:39.730
is that they're asking the partners,

00:04:39.730 --> 00:04:41.540
the local partners in Russia,

00:04:41.540 --> 00:04:45.340
to buy out the Russian
organization of Oliver Wyman

00:04:45.340 --> 00:04:47.600
and then potentially continue operating it

00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:48.960
under a different name.

00:04:48.960 --> 00:04:51.110
Now in this video, I don't
want judge these actions.

00:04:51.110 --> 00:04:53.640
I trust this might be good
news to the Russian employees

00:04:53.640 --> 00:04:56.230
as maybe likely they
will not lose their job

00:04:56.230 --> 00:04:57.550
or might not need to move

00:04:57.550 --> 00:04:59.890
to other countries, other
regions, other offices.

00:04:59.890 --> 00:05:00.810
I also understand, though,

00:05:00.810 --> 00:05:03.300
that all far there's no definite
agreement on this matter.

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:06.100
Similar to the others, currently
also released a statement

00:05:06.100 --> 00:05:08.660
that they want to stop any
work for Russian clients

00:05:08.660 --> 00:05:11.220
but do want to keep
the offices still open.

00:05:11.220 --> 00:05:12.930
So far was frankly not able to collect

00:05:12.930 --> 00:05:14.110
any insider information

00:05:14.110 --> 00:05:16.440
from any Russian employee
currently right now.

00:05:16.440 --> 00:05:18.200
So if you have anything to share on that,

00:05:18.200 --> 00:05:20.000
please leave a comment
in the comment section.

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:21.080
Next is Roland Berger.

00:05:21.080 --> 00:05:23.360
They have very much aligned
with the other companies.

00:05:23.360 --> 00:05:26.160
So they're stopping any
client activities in Russia.

00:05:26.160 --> 00:05:28.510
To my knowledge, leaving
the offices open for now.

00:05:28.510 --> 00:05:30.710
They're now relocating colleagues
mainly to the middle east

00:05:30.710 --> 00:05:32.780
and also some other international offices

00:05:32.780 --> 00:05:33.910
and helping them to get staff

00:05:33.910 --> 00:05:35.600
to international projects from there.

00:05:35.600 --> 00:05:38.180
Accenture arguably took
the most drastic measures

00:05:38.180 --> 00:05:39.780
from the companies on this list.

00:05:39.780 --> 00:05:43.296
They completely discontinued
all operations in Russia

00:05:43.296 --> 00:05:48.080
and laid off all of their
apparently 2,300 people

00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:49.270
working in that country.

00:05:49.270 --> 00:05:51.600
Overall, the whole
organization was laid off

00:05:51.600 --> 00:05:52.880
and the severance offer

00:05:52.880 --> 00:05:55.480
that these people received,
this at least what I was told,

00:05:55.480 --> 00:05:57.870
is that they got three monthly salaries

00:05:57.870 --> 00:05:59.120
as a severance payment.

00:05:59.120 --> 00:06:00.960
Let's next talk about the Big 4.

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:04.850
So this is PWC, KPMG, EY, and Deloitte.

00:06:04.850 --> 00:06:06.133
What's first important to understand is

00:06:06.133 --> 00:06:08.320
when we talk about the Big 4 firms,

00:06:08.320 --> 00:06:09.990
that due to legal regulations,

00:06:09.990 --> 00:06:11.970
also due to their audit business,

00:06:11.970 --> 00:06:14.220
they are structured in local,

00:06:14.220 --> 00:06:17.140
legally independent subsidiaries.

00:06:17.140 --> 00:06:18.930
So there is a legal entity

00:06:18.930 --> 00:06:22.750
for the Russian business for
each of these four companies.

00:06:22.750 --> 00:06:24.530
And what all of these four firms announced

00:06:24.530 --> 00:06:26.910
is that they want to stop the affiliation

00:06:26.910 --> 00:06:28.880
of the Russian entity

00:06:28.880 --> 00:06:31.530
from the global network
of any these four firms.

00:06:31.530 --> 00:06:32.400
So what this means

00:06:32.400 --> 00:06:35.807
is that the entity that was,
for instance, called PWC Russia

00:06:35.807 --> 00:06:40.010
in the future cannot
call itself PWC anymore.

00:06:40.010 --> 00:06:42.110
But that entity still exists

00:06:42.110 --> 00:06:44.290
and can still continue its operation.

00:06:44.290 --> 00:06:45.700
And I trust this is what is happening

00:06:45.700 --> 00:06:47.920
for all the four Big 4 companies.

00:06:47.920 --> 00:06:48.920
So in all fairness,

00:06:48.920 --> 00:06:51.370
given that these are
legally independent entities

00:06:51.370 --> 00:06:53.320
it probably was more or less difficult,

00:06:53.320 --> 00:06:55.120
maybe even impossible

00:06:55.120 --> 00:06:57.550
for the mother organization to completely

00:06:57.550 --> 00:07:00.220
stop the operations in this country.

00:07:00.220 --> 00:07:02.390
Of course, I'm not a legal
expert on these issues.

00:07:02.390 --> 00:07:04.200
The result surely is that these entities

00:07:04.200 --> 00:07:05.620
will continue its operations

00:07:05.620 --> 00:07:07.640
likely under a new name in the future.

00:07:07.640 --> 00:07:10.020
And I received some details
from an internal memo

00:07:10.020 --> 00:07:11.790
of one of these Russian organizations

00:07:11.790 --> 00:07:12.860
from one of these firms.

00:07:12.860 --> 00:07:14.840
And in this memo,
Russian leadership stated

00:07:14.840 --> 00:07:18.240
that they actually see the
situation from now on positively

00:07:18.240 --> 00:07:19.990
because now there will be less competition

00:07:19.990 --> 00:07:21.460
from international firms.

00:07:21.460 --> 00:07:23.070
And on top, they will
also get access to lots

00:07:23.070 --> 00:07:24.800
of talent from other consulting firms,

00:07:24.800 --> 00:07:25.920
staff that was laid off

00:07:25.920 --> 00:07:28.700
or did not want to relocate
to any other location.

00:07:28.700 --> 00:07:30.530
Those of course are people who will likely

00:07:30.530 --> 00:07:33.650
maybe want to work for any
of these firms going forward.

00:07:33.650 --> 00:07:35.080
So, interesting situation.

00:07:35.080 --> 00:07:37.170
Let me know what you think
about this in the comments.

00:07:37.170 --> 00:07:39.030
Hope this served as an
informative overview

00:07:39.030 --> 00:07:41.260
of the situation of
consulting firms in Russia.

00:07:41.260 --> 00:07:43.230
If you took any value out of this video,

00:07:43.230 --> 00:07:46.730
as always destroy the like
button for the YouTube algorithm.

00:07:46.730 --> 00:07:49.300
And also subscribe to stay
up to date on my content.

00:07:49.300 --> 00:07:50.133
Big, big thanks

00:07:50.133 --> 00:07:52.480
to the members of this
channel supporting my work.

00:07:52.480 --> 00:07:56.120
Once again, I will donate all
ad revenue from this video

00:07:56.120 --> 00:07:57.930
the UN refugee agency.

00:07:57.930 --> 00:07:58.960
My name is Heinrich.

